# Round xmuse3: Muse Spark Open's prompt pass on plan (b′) (`--place bp`: the A6000 the stage, the 3090 an expert
# tier, the host the rest), the expert stream's stage lane beside the tier against the serving default. Same binary,
# two lever arms: unset (the common rule's `admit` at bp, the ring dark) and BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=split (this tree's ring
# pass as the route GEMM over the ring's half, crate::ring_gemm, on the stage card beside the tier).
# Calibration [measured]: pp512 34.07..34.28 tok/s on plan (a) (A6000 + host, int039 6adfcd6a8, depth-serve 2 rounds,
# ~/.cache/bloomery/muse/box-muse-time.log) = 242 ms a layer a 512-row pass; less the card front ~10 ms and the join
# ~2 ms, the host union over plan (a)'s ~220..225 host experts is ~230 ms: h = 1.02..1.05 ms an expert at m = 16
# columns (XSTREAM_COSTS' t(m) = 28.1 + 57.6 m = 0.95 ms sits 7..10 % under it).
# The lane [derived from host/xstream.rs]: a fill thread copies the expert into pinned staging, then the copy engine
# reads staging over PCIe: three DRAM passes a byte (the source read, the staging write, the DMA read). One lane at
# the held rate (LANE_HELD_B_PER_US 20.41 GB/s) is 0.655 ms an expert beside the union (burst share 0.030 at m = 16);
# its DRAM is ~61 GB/s. Two lanes (this card and the 3090) would ask 122 GB/s of the host's 137 before the union's
# reads: DRAM-bound, so the 3090 lane is out of this card. muse2card B4's 158..169 assumed a raw 26.28 GB/s copy with
# no staging, a 34 us grouped GEMM and no DRAM term; it does not hold against the code.
# The rule [derived, runtime/src/xsplit.rs]: with the old card row (the `_sel` per-slot GEMV, 18.5 us a column) m* =
# 16.8 and m_min = 537 > the 512-row pass, so the ring was dark on every pass; with the route GEMM's row (20 us fixed,
# 1.6 us a column) m* = 12.1 and m_min = 386: the ring lights at 512.
# Base arm per pass and layer [derived]: host CPU, the union over ~191 host experts x 1.02..1.05 ms = 195..201 ms (the
#   bound); stage SM front ~10 ms, its ~36 `_sel` experts ~11 ms and the tier's ~29 ~9 ms under the union (0); PCIe
#   the rows and sums ~0.7 ms; DRAM 12 GB/s of 137. 207..213 ms x 62 = 12.8..13.2 s: 38.8..40.0, the call picks'
#   admits up to +10 %: 38.5..44.
# Split arm per pass and layer [derived]: the ring's room (stream_bytes, ~3.5 GB on the A6000) moves ~4 stage experts
#   a layer to the host, ~195 host experts. Balanced at H x h' = S x 0.655 ms, h' = h x 1.0..1.33 (fill threads take
#   union cores): S = 119..133 streamed, H = 76..62 on the host, T = 78..87 ms (lane-bound); the card's ring GEMM
#   S x 0.046 ms = 5.5..6.1 ms under the lane (0); DRAM 59..67 GB/s lane + 11..13 union, under 137. T + front 10 +
#   join 2 = 90..99 ms x 62 = 5.6..6.1 s: 83..92 tok/s.
# Effect: 83..92 over 38.5..44 = +89..+139 %. The rule's balance prices copy + card as a serial sum (0.70 against
# 0.655 ms), streaming ~4 % fewer than the balance: inside the band.
# Sitting (on the lead's go, both cards in the timing witness, ~13 min: 2 arms x 3 rounds, a fresh server each,
# load 40..110 s):
#   BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/xmuse3-pp.card BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090
#     DEPTH_SERVE_CTX=4224' tools/ref/depth-serve.sh <this tree>:512 env=BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=split:<this tree>:512
kind: ab
question: does the expert stream's stage lane beside the expert tier (BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=split, the ring pass as the
  route GEMM) raise the Muse Spark Open seat's prompt rate on plan (b′) over the serving default's admit?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 512, bloomery-serve --model musespark at the serving defaults (place unset -> bp), A6000 + 3090 +
  host, depth-serve rows (timings.prompt_per_second) — (split - unset) / unset, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +89..+139
rounds: 3
condition: depth-serve under BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090 in its own lease, one fresh server an arm and a round,
  the arm order rotated every round; each server's `place unset` record names bp and its `plan` record a tier0 card
  holding experts; the unset arm's `xstream=` line names admit and the split arm's split, else the row is void; the
  witness (both cards, mem, pgmajfault) shows no other model load and no row carries [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
decide-in: turn the unset rule's bp arm to split for a body whose ring runs beside its tier (the check_mode fact
  the body passes), land, and write the row beside plan (a)'s
decide-below: read the split arm's stream records (streamed experts and columns a layer, the lane's rate) against
  S = 119..133 and 0.655 ms an expert; a slower lane is the staging's DRAM passes (a registered source next), fewer
  streamed is the rule's balance
decide-above: re-derive the base: the union's per-expert cost at bp or the admits the base arm's picks made are not
  the counted ones; read the base arm's pick records before any further lever
